    <item>
      <title>Q1 2025 Grants announced</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/q1-2025-grants-announced/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 07 Apr 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/q1-2025-grants-announced/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FPA General Assembly has finalized the list of approved grant applications for the first quarter of 2025.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ajinkya Dahale&lt;/strong&gt; (AjinkyaDahale) will develop &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/33&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;two new types of curves&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in Sketcher: restricted and offset curves. Restricted curves are useful when we only need a portion of an external curve that can change. Offset curves are dependent on a parent curve to allow offset for a larger set of curves (independent offset curves already exist in FreeCAD, this is different). Ajinkya was awarded a grant of EUR 2000 for the project.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
