    <item>
      <title>New Grants: transparent preview in Part Design, interactive Sketcher tutorials</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-transparent-preview-in-part-design-interactive-sketcher-tutorials/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 02 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-transparent-preview-in-part-design-interactive-sketcher-tutorials/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FPA General Assembly approved two new grant applications.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kacper Donat&lt;/strong&gt; aka kadet will work on a &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/FreeCAD/FPA-grant-proposals/issues/22&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;new feature preview system&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; that can be used in Part and Part Design. Whenever you need to apply Pad or Loft or any other command, you will get a transparent preview of what you are getting right in the viewport.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Grants: VarSets, Mediawiki, artwork guidelines and icons</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-varsets-mediawiki-artwork-guidelines-and-icons/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 18 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-varsets-mediawiki-artwork-guidelines-and-icons/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FPA General Assembly approved three new grant applications.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pieter Hijma&lt;/strong&gt; will work on improving the user experience of VarSets. The work will include guiding the discussion on the more complicated topics, adding new features that are requested from users, and improving on various small issues. The work is scheduled to be done between January and April 2025. Pieter was awarded EUR 8,000 for the work.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>FOSDEM and KiCAD &#43; FreeCAD day 2025</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/fosdem-and-kicad-freecad-day-2025/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 04 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/fosdem-and-kicad-freecad-day-2025/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s happening again! &lt;a href=&#34;https://fosdem.org&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Fosdem&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FOSDEM 2025&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has been announced and, like the previous years, the &lt;a href=&#34;https://fpa.freecad.org&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;FPA&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are thrilled to organise once again our world-famous &lt;strong&gt;FreeCAD events&lt;/strong&gt;. These will take place in Brussels, from January 28th to February the 2nd 2025, together with FOSDEM. Be ready for several days full of coding, open-sourceness and fun!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Grants: CI hosting research, bugfixing, v1.0 teaser video</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-ci-hosting-research-bugfixing-v1-0-teaser-video/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 15 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-ci-hosting-research-bugfixing-v1-0-teaser-video/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FPA recently approved three more grants:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jackson Oursland&lt;/strong&gt; will research various options for FreeCAD to get fast CI runners. Currently, we have free runners from GitHub, but they are relatively slow and concurrency-limited. So Jackson will look into three general options: paid runners on GitHub, self-hosted runners in the cloud (AWS, Azure, GCS, maybe others), and self-hosted runners on premise. Jackson was awarded $500 for the research.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Grants approved: Variant Parts, debugging with CLion and VSCode, Homebrew build update</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-approved-variant-parts-debugging-with-clion-and-vscode-homebrew-build-update/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-approved-variant-parts-debugging-with-clion-and-vscode-homebrew-build-update/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FPA general assembly approved the funding of three more grants.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pieter Hijma&lt;/strong&gt; will be working on research for variant parts. There&amp;rsquo;s a number of FreeCAD features that require inserting copy-on-change links, such as referencing external geometry in a body for which SubShapeBinders are used in Part Design. The architecture behind the current implementation involves hidden parts and temporary files and is fragile. The workflow imposed by this architecture isn&amp;rsquo;t great either. Another domain where a better implementation is required are assemblies where you might want inserting a variation of a linked part.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Grants: further Toponaming work, better API documentation</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-approved-toponaming-api-docs/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 02 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-approved-toponaming-api-docs/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FreeCAD Project Association has just approved several more grants:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bradley McLean&lt;/strong&gt; will continue his work on the TNP migration. He will develop new code to address portions of &lt;a href=&#34;https://wiki.freecad.org/PartDesign_SubShapeBinder&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;SubShapeBinder&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and Sketcher that vary from both the code base at the time of the original TNP branch and from the current LinkStage3 branch. When no bugs are present, he will refactor code in Part and PartDesign based on discoveries during the toponaming project. This is a time commitment project with 100 hours of work scheduled. Bradley was awarded $5000 for the entire project.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Grants: Sketcher work, Toponaming, components for FreeCAD Library, User Manual Update</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-issued-by-the-freecad-project-association/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 09 Jun 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-issued-by-the-freecad-project-association/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FPA has issued several more grants. The first three are part of the new annual program.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ajinkya Dahale&lt;/strong&gt; is resuming his work on Sketcher and is making it more manageable to maintain and extend. His project has three deliverables:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>The annual Grant program is live</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/the-annual-grant-program-is-live/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 01 Mar 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/the-annual-grant-program-is-live/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The FPA is launching an annual grant program following &lt;a href=&#34;https://blog.freecad.org/2023/09/28/revamping-the-freecad-project-associations-grant-program/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;last year&amp;rsquo;s research&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. The goal is to foster rapid development of FreeCAD. To do that, the FPA will use the community&amp;rsquo;s donations to pay developers and non-programming contributors. We reserved a fund of 50,000 EUR for this in 2024. We aso encourage work on items from the &lt;a href=&#34;https://freecad.github.io/DevelopersHandbook/roadmap/&#34;&#xA;  class=&#34;external-link&#34;title=&#34;Open link&#34;&#xA;    target=&#34;_blank&#34;&#xA;    rel=&#34;external noreferrer noopener&#34;&gt;general roadmap&lt;span class=&#34;icon-external&#34;&gt;&lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;M11 7H6A2 2 0 004 9v9a2 2 0 002 2h9a2 2 0 002-2v-5&#34;/&gt;&lt;line x1=&#34;10&#34; y1=&#34;14&#34; x2=&#34;20&#34; y2=&#34;4&#34;/&gt;&lt;polyline points=&#34;15 4 20 4 20 9&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, but are also interested in grant applications exploring other possibilities.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>New Grants: electromagnetic system simulations and bug triage</title>
      <link>https://marcuspollio.github.io/FreeCAD-website/pr-69/news/new-grants-electromagnetic-system-simulations-and-bug-triage/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 27 Feb 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
